From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:20:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 110/111] Back in the editor window, the files on screen are
 checked against disk

The file watcher can miss a change, for example on network or NTFS
drives. When the window gets focus again, the tab shown in each view is
compared with its file: a tab without unsaved changes reloads silently,
one with unsaved changes shows the changed-on-disk bar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
index 903c8f6..964d5a2 100644
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -3175,6 +3175,18 @@ impl App {
             }
             Message::Focus(window_id) => {
                 if Some(window_id) == self.core.main_window_id() {
+                    // Back from another app: check the files on screen, in case the watcher
+                    // missed a change (network and NTFS drives do not always report them)
+                    let shown = match &self.split {
+                        Some(split) => vec![
+                            split.shown(views::Side::Left),
+                            split.shown(views::Side::Right),
+                        ],
+                        None => vec![Some(self.tab_model.active())],
+                    };
+                    for entity in shown.into_iter().flatten() {
+                        self.disk_check(entity);
+                    }
                     // focus the text box if context page is not shown
                     if !self.core.window.show_context {
                         return self.update_focus();
